# Keep the build context to what the image actually needs.
#
# Without this everything in the working tree is uploaded to the daemon before
# the first instruction runs: `.git` alone is 52 MB, `models/` is another 68 MB,
# and a local `.venv` can be larger than both. None of it is COPYed.
#
# Every path below is checked against the Dockerfile's COPY list. If you add a
# COPY, make sure its source is not excluded here -- the failure mode is a build
# that succeeds with a file missing, which `scripts/check_dockerfile.py` will
# catch only if the path is wrong rather than merely ignored.

.git/
.gitignore
.venv/
venv/
env/

# Bytecode and test caches: rebuilt inside the image, and stale host .pyc files
# compiled by a different Python would be actively wrong.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/

# The 68 MB Vosk acoustic model. Live speech is an optional extra (`[voice]`)
# and the image installs neither vosk nor rapidocr, so the scored engine never
# touches it -- `tests/test_asr.py` and `tests/test_ocr.py` skip via
# `importorskip`. Add `COPY models/ ./models/` and the voice extra together if
# the image ever needs to hear.
models/

# Training and sweep inputs, used by scripts/make_media.py and the ASR stability
# sweep. The image needs `media/scenarios/` and `media/undecidable/`, which the
# Dockerfile copies explicitly, and nothing else.
media/dataset/
media/speech/

# Outputs, not inputs.
runs/
deck/*.pptx
*.log

# Editor and OS noise.
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
